  "# Codegen co-scientist, iteration 23

Iteration 22 asked for a call+loop the linear scanner can complete, or
accept all-vreg for all loops. This file takes the second, because the
first is an empty set while `last-uses` is the highest instruction index
at which a vreg is a source.

Do not overwrite 04-22.

## Why the scanner cannot complete a terminating loop

`last-uses` in `kotoba-mir` reads no label and no branch target. A
terminating loop's induction variable is defined in the body (later
index) and used at the header phi (earlier index). At the phi, that
source is neither assigned nor backed, so the scanner throws
`:spill-required` and `allocate-with-policy` falls to `:all-vregs`.

`allocate-with-policy` already short-circuits `(and calls? (back-edge?))`
to all-vreg without trying the scanner. Neutralising `back-edge?` still
spill-falls back (iteration 22, override live, policy `[:all-vregs 8]`).
A non-terminating or n=0-only \"loop\" would be theater. This iteration
does not implement `:cfg-liveness`.

## Second shape

`countdown` carries only `n`. At the header: if `n` is zero, return `n`
(0); else call `id(n)`, subtract 1, jump back. Same textual last-use
hole as `count-loop`. Test:
`v3-terminating-call-loops-cannot-complete-the-scanner`. Both modules,
both with `back-edge?` rewritten to false, compile to `:all-vregs`. The
override ran (`pos? @calls`); green is not an unapplied redef.

Judah: kotoba-mir **45 tests, 1006 assertions, 0 failures**.

## Contract, not predicate removal

ADR 0012 now states `:loops-with-calls :all-vregs` as contract, and
`:terminating-loop-scanner :empty`. `back-edge?` stays. Remove it when
last-uses follow labels and back edges, not against a third loop shape.

Allocator routing is unchanged. Paper + tests only.

## Pins

Allocator code is still kotoba-mir `ac14016d` / kotoba-native `69e364e`.

- kotoba-mir `a114dd08d3c9e1edcb8f519a9c3f7faf0c6eafae` (merge of
  `agent/loop-all-vreg-contract`, feature `7c657f711712da9a97962b7cedc94a599a8947d5`).
  west-pin `2ac060c814db31574c70379c3499f7163ccb9754`
- amu not moved
- kotoba-native not moved (`69e364edf3154aa8fdf7d87535ca73179b4d2716`)

## Meta-review

- **Asking for a fixture the scanner can complete is not a measurement
  until you check whether the set is empty.** Iteration 22's Next named
  two arms; discrimination is which arm is possible.
- **A second terminating shape that also cannot complete the scanner
  licenses the contract, not a third attempt at the same empty set.**
- **Do not remove `back-edge?` because the fallback and the guard agree.**
  That was iteration 22. This iteration records why they must agree.

## Next

`:cfg-liveness` — last-uses that follow labels and back edges — or keep
all-vreg forever. Still missing: call + back-edge across a spill
(`with-scratch-tier-only` / pressure). kotoba-mir / kotoba-native still
do not execute compiled programs.

Do not chase fused-srem, extra MOV, FMA, PGO, kototama optimizer, a
timed `bench` export, or rematching leaf vs LLVM. Do not overwrite
04-22. Do not claim LLVM beaten. Do not remove `back-edge?`. Do not
implement cfg-liveness as a drive-by of this contract."}]
